# Schedule SMS message {% #schedule-sms %}
To send an scheduled SMS message, you can call the `createSms` endpoint with `scheduledAt` as a ISO 8601 date time string for the scheduled time.
{% multicode %}
```server-nodejs
const sdk = require('node-aacsearch');

// Init SDK
const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.aacsearch.io/v1')  // Your API Endpoint
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')                  // Your project ID
    .setKey('919c2d18fb5d4...a2ae413da83346ad2'); // Your secret API key

const messaging = new sdk.Messaging(client);

const message = await messaging.createSms(
    '<MESSAGE_ID>',             // messageId
    '<CONTENT>',                // content
    [],                         // topics (optional)
    [],                         // users (optional)
    [],                         // targets (optional)
    false,                      // draft (optional)
    '2025-02-13T22:01:00+0000'  // scheduledAt (optional)
);
```
```deno
import * as sdk from "npm:node-aacsearch";

const client = new sdk.Client()
    .setEndpoint('https://<REGION>.cloud.aacsearch.io/v1')  // Your API Endpoint
    .setProject('<PROJECT_ID>')                  // Your project ID
    .setKey('919c2d18fb5d4...a2ae413da83346ad2'); // Your secret API key

const messaging = new sdk.Messaging(client);

const message = await messaging.createSms(
    '<MESSAGE_ID>',             // messageId
    '<CONTENT>',                // content
    [],                         // topics (optional)
    [],                         // users (optional)
    [],                         // targets (optional)
    false,                      // draft (optional)
    '2025-02-13T22:01:00+0000'  // scheduledAt (optional)
);
```
```php
<?php

use AACSearch\Client;
use AACSearch\Services\Messaging;

